+## On-device translation
+
+Readers can translate headlines, teasers and full articles via the translate icon in the header (every page) or the "Read this article in another language" bar on article pages. Translation runs entirely in the browser using Chrome's built-in [Translator](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/translator-api) and [Language Detector](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/language-detection) APIs (Chrome 138+ desktop). Mark additional content as translatable with the `data-translatable` attribute. The chosen languages are remembered, and translation carries over as readers move between pages.
